 ## 10. F-counting as Y-axis energy analysis
 
-F-counting is not merely a pattern counter.
+F-counting is not merely a pattern counter, and it is not the same as node-counting.
+
+Node-counting is the simpler operation: detect structural nodes and count them. It is useful because nodes create the X-axis map. But node-counting alone can be dangerously early. It may say that price has already produced several extremes, while F-counting may say that those extremes are still only the internal anatomy of a newly forming F structure.
+
+F-counting is the more dynamic layer. It asks how nodes combine into a live structural phase.
+
+A practical example:
+
+- node 1 appears;
+- node 2 appears;
+- the trader who only counts nodes may already feel that the move is extended;
+- but from an F-counting perspective, those two nodes may only be the preparation of one Flag unit;
+- only after the third structural event or confirmation does the system say that F1 is established.
+
+This was the missing knowledge in the older simple node-counting model. The system could fade too early because it treated raw node count as overextension, while the correct F-count would have said: the first F has only just become valid.
 
 In this philosophy, F-counting becomes the primary Y-axis tool for reading energy, moment, and state.
 
